# Copy to .env and adjust. All optional.

# --- FalkorDB (ephemeral review-neighborhood graphs + Browser) ---
# Uncommon 5xxxx ports to avoid clashing with other local projects.
PLEX_FALKORDB_PORT=56379
PLEX_FALKORDB_BROWSER_PORT=53000
# Tell Plex where FalkorDB is (enables the --falkor viz layer):
PLEX_FALKORDB_URL=redis://localhost:56379

# --- Kùzu Explorer (optional: browse a repo's durable code graph) ---
# Pinned to match the kuzu npm version in this repo:
KUZU_EXPLORER_TAG=0.11.3
KUZU_EXPLORER_PORT=58000
# A repo's Plex data DIR (created by `plex index <repo>`) + the db filename inside it.
# The Explorer mounts the dir and opens /database/$KUZU_FILE.
KUZU_DB_DIR=/absolute/path/to/your/repo/.plex
KUZU_FILE=graph.kuzu

# --- Plex knowledge / embeddings / mining ---
# PLEX_KNOWLEDGE_DIR=~/.plex/knowledge
# Embeddings power knowledge retrieval + mining clustering. Required for those features
# (default is none → knowledge stays disabled until set). Pick ONE and set its key:
# PLEX_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=voyage        # voyage | openai | gemini | ollama
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=...                    # voyage-code-3 (code-specialized; recommended)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=...                    # text-embedding-3-small
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...                    # gemini-embedding-001
#   (ollama needs no key — runs locally: nomic-embed-text)
# NOTE: switching providers means re-embedding (`plex mine --reset` / re-seed) — vectors
# from different models are not comparable.
# PLEX_LLM_PROVIDER=claude-cli          # mining distiller: claude-cli (default) | anthropic | openai
